  "seoBody": "<p>A compliance certificate says a system, installation or item of equipment meets a standard. With Quickler you answer the questions on site in WhatsApp, and it makes the PDF certificate.</p><h2>Any trade that issues a certificate.</h2><p>Certificates show that work meets a recognised standard. Examples:</p><ul><li>Electrical installation condition reports (EICRs)</li><li>Gas safety certificates (CP12)</li><li>Structural survey completion records</li></ul><p>Insurers, regulators and clients ask for them. Issuing one without a record of the inspection behind it is a risk.</p><h2>What the paper way costs.</h2><ul><li>You fill a paper form on site.</li><li>You photograph it and email the office.</li><li>Someone retypes it into a template.</li><li>They email the certificate and file it.</li></ul><p>With Quickler you answer in WhatsApp. The certificate is made for you. The PDF lands in the manager's inbox.</p><h2>One-click approval from the email. No login.</h2><h3>Certificate, summary and button</h3><p>The manager gets the PDF, a summary of key answers and flagged items, and one approve button.</p><h3>Approve from the email</h3><p>One click marks the certificate signed off and times it. No login.</p><h2>Common questions.</h2><h3>What is a compliance certificate?</h3><p>It is a formal paper that says a system, installation or item of equipment was inspected and meets a standard. Regulators, insurers and clients ask for it.</p><h3>How does Quickler write a certificate?</h3><p>Each certificate field becomes a question in WhatsApp. You answer on site by text, voice note or photo. When you say done, the PDF is made.</p><h3>Does the manager need to approve it?</h3><p>Approval is optional. Where it is on, the manager gets a one-click approve button in the email, next to the PDF. Approval is timed and kept.</p><h3>How is the certificate delivered?</h3><p>The PDF is emailed to the manager when you finish. It is also kept for download at any time.</p><h3>Is it legally valid?</h3><p>Quickler keeps a timed record of your answers and proof. Whether it is valid depends on the standard and on your qualifications. You provide the professional judgement.</p><h3>Who uses this?</h3><p>Anyone who issues a certificate at the end of a job. Examples: EICRs, gas safety records (CP12) and structural survey records.</p><h3>Can I use my own template?</h3><p>Yes. Send a certificate you already use and Quickler builds the template from it. No design work.</p>",
